## Root cause

A heap leak in the retry path of `send_with_retry()` in `main/main.c`.

The `link_send()` contract (documented in `main/link.h`) is: **on success the link takes ownership of `pkt.data` and frees it; on any error the caller keeps ownership.** The radio intentionally returns `ESP_ERR_TIMEOUT` on every 5th call (radio busy), and the code retries by allocating a fresh encoded buffer each attempt.

On the error branch the code never freed `pkt.data`, so every failed attempt leaked a `FRAME_SIZE + 8` = 4104-byte buffer. At 50 Hz with a ~20% failure rate that's ~40 KB/s of leaked heap. The `stats` line confirmed it: `heap_free` fell from 391916 → 340924 → 285960 → … ~55 KB per line. Once the heap runs dry, `encode_frame()` returns `NULL` and every send fails permanently.

## Fix

One line in `main/main.c`: free the encoded buffer when `link_send()` does not take ownership.

```c
esp_err_t err = link_send(&pkt);
if (err == ESP_OK) {
    return ESP_OK;
}
/* link_send only takes ownership on success; free the encoded buffer on error or it leaks. */
free(pkt.data);
ESP_LOGW(TAG, "send failed (%s), retrying", esp_err_to_name(err));
retries++;
```

No changes to `link.c`/`link.h`, frame size, or the 50 Hz rate.

## Verification on the board

Flashed and ran for 120 s (~6000 frames at 50 Hz):

- Before: `heap_free` dropped every stats line (391916 → 340924 → 285960 → …), then sends died.
- After: `heap_free=391916` constant on every line, `sent` climbing, `retries` climbing, `failed=0`, `queue=0` — it keeps sending indefinitely.
